From daae59c55a9a8b7e859597ee29706d0ba28a0617 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kirn Gill II <segin2005@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 10 Jun 2026 00:29:45 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 31/83] contrib/gtk1: port GTK+ 1.2.10 (Xlib GDK; libgtk +
 libgdk)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The classic GTK+ toolkit.  GDK is bundled and Xlib-only (no Cairo/Pango/
ATK), so prerequisites are just the substrate X client stack plus the
glib1 port.  build.sh assembles a sysroot from those dist trees, relocates
glib-config to emit sysroot paths, cross-configures (autoconf 2.13; sizeof/
socklen run-tests preseeded via env), builds gdk+gtk only (po/ needs a
gettext that still accepts 1999-era charset names; docs/ needs SGML tooling
— neither is runtime), and stages dist-gtk1 with the .so OSABI patched to
ELFOSABI_SUBSTRATE.

Patch 0001-ltconfig-substrate-shared: the same host_os=substrate ->
linux-gnu canonicalization as glib1, so the bundled 2001-era ltconfig emits
ELF shared libraries.  Produces gtk-config, libgtk-1.2.so, libgdk-1.2.so;
DT_NEEDED resolves entirely within the substrate stack (libgmodule/libglib,
libX11/libXext, libdl/libm/libc).

Completes the GTK+ 1.2 port (task: GTK+ 1.2 = glib1 + gtk1).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
